ir  50s but guns were found in the luggage  of an 84 year old woman a ten year old  boy an airport worker and a pastor from  Texas who told police he forgot the gun  was in his backpack  Colorado State Representative lori saine  spent a night in jail after a gun was  found in her purse at Denver  International Airport they said right  away I'm sorry I forgot I'm a mistake  and and that's when I was cuffed she was  ultimately not criminally charged but  did receive a nearly $2,000 fine from  the TSA hopefully this is a learning  experience for others not to make the  mistake in the first place the agency  can seek fines up to $13,000 in press  releases TSA says a typical first  offense draws a thirty nine hundred  dollar fine but we found on average it's  actually closer to 1100 no one last year  received the maximum TSA administrator  David pukowski the fine could be 3,900  or $4,000 but no one ever pays that on  occasion they do though we're trying to  provide that that warning if you will  that hey there is there is a penalty  here and if we can prevent it in the  first place I think that's a better  better way to approach it a review of  the police documents reveals at least  three incidents last year where it  appears the gun was missed by TSA  screeners at one Airport and only  discovered on the person's trip home how  does that happen  it happens because the technology  doesn't get everything all the time  either there's a technology issue  there's a procedural issue or there's a  training issue and a little troubled by  the fact that the gun went through the  x-ray machine and was missed  oh I'm troubled by that too I think  everybody in TSA is troubled by it and  mistakes happen  how often do those mistakes happen I  can't give you an answer as to how often  it happens but when it does happen we do  everything we can to figure out why it  happened  the TSA is starting to roll out new CT  scanners to checkpoints that should make  it easier for screeners to sp